# v6.1.2 — aarch64 EADDRA_IMM 12-bit-mask fix (>4095 byte-literal offsets).
# Issue: 2026-06-07-aarch64-eaddra-imm-12bit-mask-over-4095.md
#
# A byte-array literal with >4096 elements drives EADDRA_IMM(S, b_i) with
# b_i >= 4096 (via the peephole's correct disp>=4096 legacy fallback).
# Pre-fix, aarch64 masked the operand to 12 bits → `add x0,x0,#(b_i&0xFFF)`,
# so b_i==4096 → `add #0` → the byte was written to &huge+0 (silent
# corruption). x86 was always correct (full disp32). This test passes
# trivially on x86 and is the regression guard for aarch64 (run under
# qemu-aarch64 / on pi+ecb). Markers at the 4096 boundary (hi-chunk=1) and
# 8192 (hi-chunk=2, LSL#12 imm=2).

include "lib/syscalls.cyr"
include "lib/alloc.cyr"
include "lib/fmt.cyr"
include "lib/assert.cyr"

